# Repo-root .dockerignore — only deploy/frontend/Dockerfile currently uses
# the repo root as its build context (see docker-compose.oracle.yml's
# `frontend.build.context: ../..`); every other service's context is
# scoped to its own subdirectory. Without this file, `docker build` was
# packing the *entire* monorepo (~6.8GB, including other packages'
# node_modules/.venv and .git history) into the build context on every
# frontend build — none of which the Dockerfile's COPY instructions
# actually need, since npm ci reinstalls dependencies fresh inside the
# image. Trimming this is what "context" cleanup refers to in the M3.1
# production build hotfix.
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/dist/
**/.expo/
**/web-build/
**/expo-env.d.ts
rag-backend/data/
